WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.801
Special Counsel Jack Smith making rare

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.236
public remarks on Friday

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.871
after unsealing the historic

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:05.905
40 plus page

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.741
federal indictment of former president

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.143
and current 2024 candidate Donald Trump.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:14.047
My office will seek a speedy trial

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:15.382
in this matter

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:16.950
consistent with the public interest

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.053
and the rights of the accused

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.621
We very much look forward

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.189
to presenting our case

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.824
to a jury of citizens

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.660
in the Southern District of Florida.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.095
Smith did not go into details

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:29.662
of the indictment,

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.564
but said people ought to read it.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:32.599
Joining me now is Ellie

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.733
Honig, CNN's senior

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.468
legal analyst, former assistant U.S.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.169
attorney

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.837
for the Southern District of New York.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.506
So great to have you back Ellie.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.408
Let's talk about big picture.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:43.576
First of all, he's investigating.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:44.878
He, Jack Smith, both

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:48.481
January six and Mar a Lago documents.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:49.682
What do you make of the fact

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.484
that this was an indictment pertaining to

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.852
one and not the other?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:54.421
Well, Michael, and

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.321
let's keep in mind, Mar

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.757
a Lago has essentially lapsed January 6th

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.892
because DOJ

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.660
even before Jack Smith was appointed.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.395
They purportedly have been investigating

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:03.363
January six, essentially

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.264
since it happened.

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.099
So we are two and a half years out.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:06.866
Mar a Lago really

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:07.767
didn't surface

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.335
until the search warrant hit

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.737
almost a year ago.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.172
So what this tells me, obviously,

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:13.973
we now have an indictment on the Mar

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:14.741
a Lago documents.

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:15.842
We'll talk more about that.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.845
January six is still ongoing at DOJ

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.014
I don't think there's much of a

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.315
realistic possibility

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.385
that it gets charged by DOJ anytime soon.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.853
And one indicator of that is

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:29.222
we've not seen any progress really.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.657
We've not seen anybody

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:32.225
close to Donald Trump being charged.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:32.559
Remember,

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:33.426
there's a whole sort of

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.894
secondary cast of characters

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.563
around Trump on January six.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.631
Jeffrey Clark, John Eastman,

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.433
no movement towards any of them.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.569
So there's been sort of radio silence

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.636
that's still pending.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:44.637
But it wouldn't surprise me

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.072
if the ultimate decision from DOJ

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.240
is no charge against Trump.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.442
On January six, Right.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.311
I guess that's really what I was asking.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.712
Do you read into this

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.481
that maybe Trump is getting a pass

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.883
in the eyes of DOJ for January six?

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.017
Or is it that

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.053
this is a much more straightforward case?

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.055
Well, I think it's both.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.389
I think this case

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.557
and I think the indictment

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.860
is fairly straightforward and well done.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.528
And I think it makes sense to me

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:09.929
that this was charged more quickly.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.598
I also think that the charging

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:13.099
of this case gives Merrick Garland

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.834
perhaps some political cover

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.669
if he ends up not charging.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.337
January six,

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.805
I know we see Garland and Jack Smith

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.807
as these sort of nonpolitical icons,

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.575
but they're aware of public perception.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.077
They understand that it's important

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:26.079
that DOJ be seen as fair.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:26.779
And I think

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.748
ultimately if Garland does not charge

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:29.749
on January six,

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:30.884
people who would be upset by

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:32.252
that may look at the charge

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.920
we saw this week and think, well,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.022
at least he charged one of those cases.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.190
Okay.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.124
I'm glad you brought up

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:39.692
Merrick Garland, the attorney general,

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.094
because previously here

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:41.928
you and I have talked

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:42.695
about the concept

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.964
of prosecutorial discretion.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.599
I made the argument that I had

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:47.000
I thought

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.902
Smith had a very straightforward task,

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.403
but that there was some question

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:50.670
as to

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.638
whether Merrick Garland

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.006
would accept the recommendation

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:53.706
that he was provided

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.241
by the special counsel.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.111
This is Merrick Garland decision, right?

00:02:58.978 --> 00:02:59.546
Yes.

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.613
Ultimately, it's Merrick

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.347
Garland decision.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.815
The way it works under the regulations

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.017
is the special counsel.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:06.119
Jack Smith has control of his day

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.320
to day investigation.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.922
It's supposed to be hands off,

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:10.256
but at a certain point,

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.958
the special counsel has to run

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.493
a potential indictment or decision

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:14.160
not to indict.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.562
That absolutely by law,

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:17.030
has to go to the attorney general,

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.598
who then has to defer

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.532
not automatically,

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.568
but has to generally defer towards

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:23.036
what the special counsel wants.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.504
So we know for sure

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.406
that Jack Smith recommended an indictment

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.308
And we know for sure that Merrick Garland

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.475
approved it. And I agree with you.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:30.843
I think Merrick Garland, as the A.G.,

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.312
has to take a broader look

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.479
and has to think about the broader

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.514
political picture.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:35.949
And we now know the end result of

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:36.649
that calculus.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:38.351
I said

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.652
in my opening commentary today

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:40.453
that the photographs

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.088
contained in the indictment

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:42.655
and by the way,

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:43.122
I want to know

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.290
how rare that you would see

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.259
pictures in an indictment like this.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:46.793
Put that one

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:47.327
up, Katherine,

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:49.229
that I call the Rorschach test,

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.930
because, you know, to some there it is.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:51.631
You look at it

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.799
and it's stuff is spread

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:53.433
out on the floor,

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:53.766
like, oh,

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:54.334
my God,

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.635
is this the careless way

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:56.402
with which

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.937
he was treating these documents?

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.006
And then Trump's response is to say,

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.941
who spread that stuff on the floor?

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:02.642
And by the way,

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.543
all I see,

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.611
according to Trump,

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:06.112
our newspaper headlines.

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:08.281
What's the impact of what I'm showing

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:08.815
right now?

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:11.117
You know, the pictures to which I refer.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:11.551
I do.

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:11.851
Yeah.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:12.952
So, first of all, you're right, Michael.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:13.953
It's sort of a new thing

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.421
to have photographs and indictments

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.990
I remember seeing the first one

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.424
maybe five years ago

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.325
when I was just getting ready

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:20.493
to leave a prosecutor's office

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.060
and thought, well,

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.629
you can put a photo in an indictment.

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:23.997
It was unthinkable to me.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.531
This traditional prosecutor

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.566
and now they're there all the time

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:27.667
and they should be there evidence.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:28.835
Why not?

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.203
It's such an interesting Rorschach test,

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:31.504
but I'm not really buying the.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:32.839
Well, they're just newspaper side.

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.140
Yes, they are just newspapers.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.375
But the fact that

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:36.309
some or perhaps

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:37.543
many of the documents

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:40.079
were innocuous or souvenirs, fine.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.547
That doesn't undermine

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:41.948
the fact

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.916
that even a small portion of them

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.285
were decidedly not

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.119
And the indictment

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:46.953
lays out

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:47.854
the high level

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.889
of sensitivity of those documents.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:50.890
So it doesn't much matter to me

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.091
if the sensitive documents

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.593
are all alone in one folder

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:55.461
or are surrounded by tchotchkes.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.330
Is, to use your excellent phrase

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.031
from earlier,

00:04:58.031 --> 00:04:59.966
it's the ones that are sensitive that we

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:00.700
care about here.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.136
Jack Smith says he wants

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.537
to give them a speedy trial.

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:06.339
Is that going to happen?

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:10.310
Not by the legal definition of speedy.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.011
So the federal rules say

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:12.745
that a defendant

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:15.381
is entitled to be tried within 70

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:17.417
70 days of an indictment.

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:18.151
Michael, no

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:18.785
federal case

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:21.788
ever gets tried anywhere near 70 days.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:22.455
The thing

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.523
that's important to note here, though,

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:26.326
is it's not really up to Jack Smith

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:27.427
when the trial happens.

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:28.394
Jack Smith was just

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:29.028
saying the thing

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.129
that all good prosecutors

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.264
are trying to say

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:32.832
you are sort of trained from day one.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.300
If a judge said to me today,

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.435
you have to go to trial tomorrow

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:35.968
at 9 a.m.,

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.170
I would say we're ready for trial

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:37.537
your honor.

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.038
That's just you automatically say that

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:40.740
that's always your position really.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.407
Who governs

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:44.043
when trial happens is a the judge

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.511
but with more deference

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:46.579
towards the defendant

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:47.580
because the defendant's

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.549
the one with constitutional rights,

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.684
with the ability to bring motions,

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.853
with the need to prepare his defense

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.388
to do his own investigation,

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:56.656
the defense is just starting

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:57.523
their investigation

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.991
theoretically on the day

00:05:58.991 --> 00:05:59.792
they get the indictment.

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:00.393
So Jeff

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.128
Smith is just saying we're ready to go

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:02.795
as soon as possible.

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:04.063
I think that's an important message

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:04.664
to send.

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:06.632
But ultimately, he doesn't control that.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.968
Ellie, on my

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.336
civil side of the aisle,

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:11.771
I know a thing or two

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:12.772
when I have a choice

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:15.108
of of venue, juristic motion

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:16.042
where I'm going.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.610
I'm looking for a friendly plaintiff

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.311
audience.

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:19.712
In this case,

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.514
Jack Smith could have brought charges

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:22.548
in D.C.. Right.

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.550
But instead goes to Florida

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:26.319
which I guess by rights is where

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:27.954
most of the conduct occurred.

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:29.856
But you would think, politically

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:30.490
speaking, it's

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.791
a more hospitable

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:34.494
jury for Donald Trump down South

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:38.364
This is the single most consequential

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:39.632
turn of the week

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:40.833
other than the indictment itself

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.402
dropping and really a shocker

00:06:42.402 --> 00:06:44.570
because up until three or four days ago,

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.705
everything was in D.C.

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:46.472
The team,

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:47.907
the prosecution team was in D.C.,

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.776
the grand jury was in D.C.

00:06:49.776 --> 00:06:50.443
and it looked like

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:51.677
they were going to charge in D.C.

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:52.178
And you're right,

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:54.313
there's an enormous difference

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:55.581
in the jury pools here.

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.449
D.C.,

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:57.049
Donald Trump

00:06:57.049 --> 00:07:00.453
got 5%, just over 5% of the vote in 2020

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:02.955
meaning about 95% of the people

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.123
who would have been in that jury pool

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:04.857
in D.C.

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:05.792
voted against him.

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:08.728
Of course, Trump won Florida in 2020

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:10.062
most of the southern counties

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:10.997
where this is going to

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:11.964
draw its jury pool for him

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:13.499
he won at least 40%.

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:15.735
So you're looking at a very different

00:07:15.735 --> 00:07:16.302
jury pool.

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:17.203
And people will say,

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:18.604
well jurors are instructed

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:19.372
they're selected.

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:20.740
They're sort of vetted out

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:21.941
and they're told don't

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:23.109
bring your political views

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:24.944
into the courtroom Nonsense.

00:07:24.944 --> 00:07:26.279
I've tried enough cases.

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:27.380
Jurors are human beings,

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.514
and especially in Donald Trump.

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.082
I'm not saying it's impossible

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:31.350
that somebody who likes Trump votes

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.618
to convict him or vice versa.

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:33.853
But Man-To-Man

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:35.822
do you want to be in front of a jury

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:36.756
that doesn't like the guy?

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:38.991
And let me say, I give DOJ credit here.

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:40.693
They did the right thing legally

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:41.394
because they

00:07:41.394 --> 00:07:42.662
definitely have

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:44.430
proper venue down in Florida,

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:44.764
